# Epoch 3 Dynamo Crawler — fidelity and presentation

Branch: `sol/boss-art-fidelity-review`, base `d41ab98ce`. Work dated 2026-09-08. No commit or deployment.

**Verdict: IN PROGRESS — asset verified; runtime acceptance pending.** E1 and E2 are verified. This report records E3's completed asset work and outstanding runtime checks; it does not close the ten-epoch goal.

[Comparison gallery](../artifacts/boss-fidelity/e3-crawler/index.html) · [form reference](../assets/raw/plate-e3-boss-dynamo-crawler.png)

## Changes and rationale

The baseline hid its drive wheels behind broad skirts and reduced the electrical mast to a ladder with small ceramic buttons. Shorter skirts expose existing wheels inside the required treads. Three substantial collared teal chambers, two horizontal connections and a forward collector restore the electrical-machine silhouette. Unequal stacks, wound copper capacitors, broad caps, curved upper conduits, lower caged chambers and framed dynamo windows recover the main features of the source illustration.

A native-generated eight-region atlas replaces the procedural brown striping. Primitive cylinder UVs keep copper windings horizontal. The original plate remains the form reference; no external 3D service is used. The six capacitors and three original damage components remain. Hidden rupture cores were moved inside the revised jars, and their damage transforms were updated with them. Small rivets and hidden underside bevels give up geometry to the more visible machinery within the existing ceiling.

The illustrated rail wheels and gameplay-required treads are an existing discrepancy. This pass retains the treads and exposes their wheel rhythm. Fine engraved metalwork, the dense radial boiler assembly and luminous lower plumbing remain simplified; the improvement is not a claim of exact reproduction.

## Verified asset evidence

| Property | Final candidate |
|---|---|
| Geometry | 11,760 triangles, down from 11,980; ceiling 12,000 |
| Bounds, length × height × width | 3.20 × 2.6775 × 1.34; centered grounded base |
| Components | Three original mesh names, one original damage morph each |
| Surface | One material, one embedded 1024×1024 PNG atlas |
| GLB bytes | 3,205,932 |
| SHA-256 | `26112eaa095aa891d57c209e224e81a3a9fc89bc6f56614eb98ee6d5d5016eb6` |
| Reproducibility | Saved-Blend re-export and three fresh source builds are byte-identical |
| Beam attachment | `drain_mast` node extras record intact and damaged local collector centers derived from actual vertices |

See [export contract](../assets/pilots/crawler-3d/renders/crawler-asset-contract.json), [verification log](../artifacts/boss-fidelity/e3-crawler/verify.log), [fresh-build receipt](../artifacts/boss-fidelity/e3-crawler/source-determinism.json) and [native provenance](../assets/layer-contracts/crawler.v1.json).

Independent source review found no introduced bug in the builder/verifier. It checked atlas regions, copper winding orientation, hidden damage volumes, unchanged normalization, damage pivots and authored collector anchors. Its independent three fresh exports match the same hash. [Review log](../artifacts/boss-fidelity/e3-crawler/asset-review.log).

Independent visual inspection found no malformed base geometry or destructive mesh deformation. The [full damage board](../artifacts/boss-fidelity/e3-crawler/candidate-neutral/crawler-full-damage-states.png) includes the fallen collector that the original review camera cropped. Remaining visual priorities concern material separation and source-detail density, rather than malformed geometry.

## Runtime findings under correction

- **F-E3-01 — model/target scale mismatch.** At the previous unit scale, front and rear target centers fall approximately 2.76 and 2.40 world units beyond their visible component triangles. Their hit radii are 0.72. A rigidly aligned larger visual model is being evaluated against unchanged combat positions, multiple acts, component loss and mobile framing.
- **F-E3-02 — floating beam attachment.** The old endpoint was a fixed height above the combat proxy. The revised render endpoint follows the authored collector center through its morph and world transform. Drain targets, power commands and damage are unchanged.
- **F-E3-03 — runtime surfaces too dark.** Preliminary white mapped fill preserves the texture but leaves the boiler and running gear difficult to see. Compare settled runtime frames before selecting scale and fill. Avoid accepting enlarged dark shapes as improved detail.
- **F-E3-04 — enlarged-model grounding and indicators.** A larger chassis needs terrain support and a health bar above its actual visual bounds. Burst-dial placement and late GLB arrival after component loss must remain coherent. These checks are pending.

## Acceptance still required

Final desktop/mobile intact and damaged frames, target overlap and terrain support across acts, late-load and component-loss placement, beam/dial/bar placement, unchanged simulation snapshots, existing lifecycle/encounter checks, a final build and independent runtime source review. The lite/procedural fallback and final roost wreck retain their existing encounter roles.
